@Mcp_HostAddress = http://localhost:4002
@accessToken = replace-with-a-bearer-token

### Issue a key
POST {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/api/agent-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Claude Desktop",
  "access": "ReadOnly"
}

### Issue a key with an expiry
POST {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/api/agent-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Temporary automation",
  "access": "Write",
  "expiresAt": "2026-12-31T00:00:00Z"
}

### List the caller's own keys
GET {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/api/agent-keys?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### List another user's keys — administrator only (403 for anyone else)
GET {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/api/agent-keys?page=1&pageSize=10&userId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Revoke a key
DELETE {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/api/agent-keys/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Revoke a key that isn't the caller's and the caller isn't an admin (404)
DELETE {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/api/agent-keys/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### No token at all (401)
GET {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/api/agent-keys?page=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

### --- MCP transport, /mcp (Streamable HTTP, stateless) ---
### Every request below needs both Accept headers — the transport answers with an
### `event: message` / `data: {...}` SSE frame even for a single response.
@agentKey = replace-with-a-pgk_-key-from-the-issue-request-above

### Initialize a session
POST {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{agentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2025-06-18",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": { "name": "Mcp.http", "version": "1.0" }
  }
}

### List tools — role, account capability, and key access are all enforced
POST {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{agentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 2,
  "method": "tools/list",
  "params": {}
}

### Assign a saved role to one connection (null resumes inheritance)
PUT {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/api/agent-keys/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/role
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"accessRoleId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"}

### Read this account's notification preferences (requires get_my_notification_preferences)
POST {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{agentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 3,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": { "name": "get_my_notification_preferences", "arguments": {} }
}

### List catalog products (requires list_products; costs only with sales.manage on the connection)
POST {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{agentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 5,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": { "name": "list_products", "arguments": { "keyword": "sofa", "pageSize": 10 } }
}

### Search an area with arguments (requires search_area)
POST {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{agentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 4,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "search_area",
    "arguments": { "query": "Seattle", "limit": 10 }
  }
}

### A direct call without list_email_templates permission is denied, even when the name is known
POST {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{agentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 5,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "list_email_templates",
    "arguments": {}
  }
}

### An unmarked tool cannot be called directly
POST {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{agentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 6,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "whoami",
    "arguments": {}
  }
}

### A JWT access token is rejected at /mcp (401) — the two credentials are scoped to their own surface
POST {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 7,
  "method": "tools/list",
  "params": {}
}

### No token at all is rejected at /mcp (401)
POST {{Mcp_HostAddress}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 8,
  "method": "tools/list",
  "params": {}
}
